{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nDiscovered while fixing `b2ff-2588-9bb7-4bd2` (change 2662), which closed the\nempty-string hole for the BOOLEAN class by making `_as_bool(\"\")` raise. That fix covers\nall 27 boolean config keys. AC5 of that bug asked for one pass over ALL config keys for\nother places `\"\"` resolves in an unsafe direction. This ticket carries the residue.\n\n## Post-fix sweep: `\"\"` through every coercer in `_config_sections._SECTIONS`\n\n67 of 104 keys now RAISE on `\"\"` — every bool, int, float, `_as_choice`, `_as_git_ref`,\n`_as_git_remote`, `_as_tracker_dir`. Those are done. 37 keys still accept it:\n\n- **27 `_as_str` keys -> `\"\"`**\n- **7 `_as_str_tuple` keys -> `()`**\n- **2 `_as_str_list` keys -> `[]`** (`code_health.scan_roots`, `include_extensions`)\n- **1 with a literal fallback** (`ticket.display_mode` -> `\"auto\"`)\n\n## Already safe — verified at the CONSUMER, not assumed\n\n- `mcp.http_allowed_hosts` / `http_allowed_origins`: an empty allowlist on a\n  non-loopback bind raises `McpStartupError` (`mcp_server.py` ~:518). Fails closed.\n- `mcp.auth_jwt_algorithms`: empty raises `AuthConfigError`\n  (`_mcp_auth.py:265`). Fails closed.\n- `jira.url` / `jira.user` / `jira.project` / `reconciler.base_url`: empty leaves the\n  integration unconfigured, so operations fail rather than proceed.\n- `reconciler.ca_bundle`: empty = system trust store, not a relaxation.\n\n## The residue that needs a disposition\n\nThese are keys where an env `\"\"` DEFEATS a file-set value in the protection direction.\nEach is a \"the operator configured a control, an expanded-to-nothing `${VAR}` removed\nit\" shape — the same mechanism as the original bug:\n\n- `verify.require_environment` — empty = op-cert environment binding OFF\n- `verify.opcert_enforce_since` — empty = no enforcement floor\n- `identity.enforce_since` — empty = no identity enforcement floor\n- `mcp.auth_required_scopes` — empty tuple -> `required_scopes=None`\n  (`mcp_server.py:577`), i.e. no scope requirement\n- `mcp.auth_jwt_expected_typ` — empty = no `typ` header check\n\n## Why this is NOT just \"make `_as_str` raise on empty\"\n\nFor several of these keys `\"\"` is the DOCUMENTED \"off\"/unset spelling and equals the\nbuilt-in default (`verify.require_environment` is empty in the committed `rebar.toml`),\nso a blanket raise would break the normal configuration. The boolean fix worked because\n`\"\"` was never a legitimate boolean; that argument does not transfer. The likely correct\nshape is a per-key declaration of whether empty is MEANINGFUL or a FAULT, applied in the\nenv layer rather than in the coercer.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Each of the five listed keys gets an explicit disposition: empty is meaningful\n      (documented) or empty is a fault (raises).\n- [x] Whatever mechanism is chosen is declarative per key, not a blanket rule over\n      `_as_str` / `_as_str_tuple` — a blanket rule breaks the documented empty defaults.\n- [x] A regression test drives the real resolver with `\"\"` against a file setting the\n      opposite for every key whose disposition is \"fault\", and pins the \"meaningful\"\n      ones as still accepting empty.\n- [x] The already-safe keys above keep their current consumer-side fail-closed\n      behaviour; the fix must not move that check out of the consumer.\n\n## Completion evidence 2026-09-07\n\n- The five protection-direction residue keys are explicitly declared in `_EMPTY_ENV_FAULT_KEYS` and now reject present-but-empty env overrides: `verify.require_environment`, `verify.opcert_enforce_since`, `identity.enforce_since`, `mcp.auth_required_scopes`, and `mcp.auth_jwt_expected_typ`.\n- The mechanism is per-key and env-layer-only (`source == \"env\"`); `_as_str` and `_as_str_tuple` remain permissive for file/default values.\n- Regression coverage in `tests/unit/test_config_empty_env_bool_b2ff.py` drives the real resolver against file values plus empty env overrides for each fault key, verifies non-empty env still overrides, and pins representative meaningful-empty policies (`ticket.default_assignee`, `ticket.display_mode`, `mcp.auth_proxy_scopes`).\n- The already-safe consumer-side checks are untouched; implementation changed only `_config_sections.py` env-layer coercion.\n- Verification: targeted `pytest tests/unit/test_config_empty_env_bool_b2ff.py -q` passed (100 tests); ruff and complexity check passed; full `make verify` passed; Gerrit change 2746 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and was submitted as 188dc1e8a0ebe27ece397012bcfe6df286a00a91.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788771355447880001,"uuid":"a05ec23b-fb47-45d8-8b51-2fdb36dccd89"}